docs: describe the real auth, and record the JWT-session constraint

README still claimed sign-in was a mock credentials flow, and
ARCHITECTURE listed email + password as the plan. Both are now Google
via Auth.js, verified in production.

Replaces the old "Credentials forces JWT sessions" constraint, which
described a provider that no longer exists, with the actual reason
sessions are JWTs: middleware has to verify them in the edge runtime,
and a database session cannot be checked there.
